        "titolo_orig": "UK: No 10 had \"dismissive attitude\" to Mandelson's vetting",
        "testo_it": "Regno Unito: polemiche a Downing Street per l'atteggiamento sprezzante verso il controllo dei precedenti di Mandelson.",
        "priorita": "Bassa",
        "id_gruppo": 10,
        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/uk-no-10-had-dismissive-attitude-to-mandelson-s-vetting",
        "orario": "18:14",
        "timestamp": 1776788075,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. UK: No 10 had \"dismissive attitude\" to Mandelson's vetting UK Issued on: 21/04/2026 - 18:14 A former senior British Foreign Office official says he was under “constant pressure” from the Prime Minister’s office to speed up Peter Mandelson’s appointment as ambassador to the US, escalating a political row that is now threatening Keir Starmer’s leadership. Olly Robbins, the department’s most senior official until his dismissal last week, told a parliamentary committee that Number 10 showed a “dismissive attitude” toward security vetting for the appointment. It follows reports that independent officials recommended denying Mandelson clearance due to his past links to Jeffrey Epstein, prompting renewed calls for Starmer to resign after he insisted due process had been followed. Olly Robbins revelas \"constant pressure\" 21/04/2026 UK Starmer’s Mandelson 'gamble': Did political firepower trump diplomacy to appease Washington? 20/04/2026 UK Pro-Palestinian rally in London: Over 500 arrested 12/04/2026 UK Deep Purple rocks Japanese PM's office 11/04/2026 JAPAN UK police investigates arson attack against Jewish charity ambulances 23/03/2026 UK Russia fatally 'poisoned' Putin critic Navalny with rare toxin, UK says 14/02/2026 RUSSIA Denis MacShane: Starmer toast? \"He's definitely in the toaster\" 08/02/2026 UK Starmer faces pressure as McSweeney resigns: Police throw curveball on files 08/02/2026 UK John McTernan: Mandelson sharing sensitive information with Epstein \"feels treasonous\" 07/02/2026 UK"
